\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Symbolic Control Synthesis for DC Motor Drive Safety
\f1\b0\fs32 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Objective:
\f1\b0  To design a supervisory control system that guarantees safe motor operation within thermal and current limits, abstract the DC motor's continuous dynamics (electrical, mechanical, and thermal) into a 
\f0\b finite symbolic transition system
\f1\b0  and synthesize a provably safe controller.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (a) State and Input Abstraction (X,U):
\f1\b0  Define the finite symbolic sets by quantizing the continuous operating ranges of the three core variables:
\fs24 \
\

\fs32 \

\f2\i Variable
\f3\b 						
\f2\b0 Continuous Role				Symbolic Set Definition\

\f1\i0 \

\f0\b Speed (\uc0\u969 )						
\f1\b0 Regulated Output			\{IDLE, LOW, NOMINAL, MAX\}
\f0\b \
Temperature (Tw )				
\f1\b0 Protection State 				\{SAFE, HOT\'a0(DERATE), OVERHEAT\'a0(TRIP)\} \

\f0\b Voltage Command (Va  / PWM)	
\f1\b0 Control Input				\{OFF,REDUCE,MAINTAIN,INCREASE\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\b \cf0 (b) Formal Safety and Target Specification:
\f5\b0  Define the critical sets governing the protection logic:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f4\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Unsafe Set (Xunsafe ):
\f5\b0  Any state where Tw = OVERHEAT or the predicted current exceeds the fixed locked-rotor limit.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Target Set (Xtarget ):
\f5\b0  The set of states where \uc0\u969 =NOMINAL AND Tw =SAFE.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Cooling Set (Xcooldown ):
\f5\b0  A set of states where the motor must remain \uc0\u969 =IDLE until Tw  drops back to SAFE(mimicking the cooling-down logic).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b \cf0 (c) Supervisory Controller Synthesis (\uc0\u948 ):
\f5\b0  Synthesize the optimal 
\f4\b Symbolic Controller (\uc0\u948 :X\u8594 U)
\f5\b0  that ensures the following temporal properties are met:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f4\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Safety:
\f5\b0  The system 
\f4\b never
\f5\b0  enters Xunsafe .\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reachability:
\f5\b0  From any safe starting state, the system 
\f4\b eventually
\f5\b0  reaches and stays within Xtarget  OR Xcooldown when thermal constraints are violated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b \cf0 (d) Overload and Locked-Rotor Action:
\f5\b0  Determine the necessary symbolic action u 
\f6 \uc0\u8712 
\f5  U to transition the system immediately from the locked-rotor condition (where ia  is maximized) to a safe state, demonstrating the controller's ability to enforce the 
\f4\b current limit
\f5\b0  protection objective.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b\fs36 \cf0 References
\f5\b0\fs32 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

